{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Goblin Salvage Project: the client gets an Item.dbc row for each new quest item",
  "contract": [
    "Requires CoA.SendDisplayPatches=1 (the default).",
    "The 3.3.5a client draws an item's bag icon from its own Item.dbc row, not from the item query answer. Items 9707001-9707008 are new, so the client has no row for them and showed a question mark.",
    "rev_20261023_50 adds their item_dbc rows and the core registers the ids, so the item query answer is followed by SMSG_PATCH_ITEM (2354): ID, ClassID, SubclassID, sound override, material, DisplayInfoID, InventoryType and SheatheType. Each display is one the client's ItemDisplayInfo.dbc already has.",
    "These are data assertions on the bytes the server sends; the harness cannot see the drawn icon."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 60000,
  "location": {
    "map": 0,
    "x": -11307.4,
    "y": -191.2,
    "z": 75.35,
    "o": 1.95
  },
  "players": [
    {
      "id": "c",
      "race": 7,
      "class": 1,
      "level": 35
    }
  ],
